prompts:
- id: a40-senior-001
  name: A-40 External Signal Coordination - Full Schema (Opportunity, Citation, Lifecycle Log)
  prompt: "Read SCHEMA_REGISTRY.md, AGENTS.md, STATE_OF_THE_BUILD.md, and src/lib/agents/a-45-backlink-intelligence-engine.ts and src/lib/agents/a-13-brand-mention-tracker.ts (both built earlier this session - confirm they exist, if either does not exist yet, stop and report which is missing since A-40 genuinely depends on both) first.\n\nMISSION (per full operator spec): A-40 discovers, coordinates, prioritizes, and tracks legitimate external authority opportunities - chambers of commerce, trade associations, manufacturer directories, supplier directories, professional organizations, municipal resources, sponsorships, trade publications. It validates every opportunity before recommending, rejects link farms and spam directories, coordinates with A-45's backlink intelligence and A-13's unlinked-mention detection, and tracks a full opportunity lifecycle from discovery through live/rejected/expired.\n\nDATA MODEL:\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS external_signal_opportunity (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  client_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES clients(id),\n  opportunity_source text NOT NULL CHECK (opportunity_source IN ('chamber_of_commerce','trade_association','manufacturer_directory','supplier_directory','professional_organization','municipal_resource','sponsorship','trade_publication','industry_directory','discovered_generic')),\n  organization_name text NOT NULL,\n  target_url text,\n  legitimacy_score numeric(4,3) NOT NULL,\n  relevance_score numeric(4,3) NOT NULL,\n  geographic_strength_score numeric(4,3),\n  topical_strength_score numeric(4,3),\n  authority_score numeric(4,3),\n  expected_seo_value_score numeric(4,3),\n  difficulty_score numeric(4,3),\n  cost_estimate_usd numeric(10,2),\n  compliance_risk_score numeric(4,3) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  composite_priority_score numeric(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  lifecycle_status text NOT NULL DEFAULT 'discovered' CHECK (lifecycle_status IN ('discovered','validated','prioritized','operator_action_required','submitted','pending','approved','live','rejected','expired')),\n  requires_human_action boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false,\n  human_action_detail text,\n  discovered_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),\n  last_revalidated_at timestamptz\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS citation_consistency_check (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  client_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES clients(id),\n  source_name text NOT NULL,\n  nap_name_matches boolean NOT NULL,\n  nap_address_matches boolean NOT NULL,\n  nap_phone_matches boolean NOT NULL,\n  discrepancy_detail jsonb,\n  checked_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS external_signal_lifecycle_log (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  opportunity_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES external_signal_opportunity(id),\n  from_status text,\n  to_status text NOT NULL,\n  changed_by text NOT NULL CHECK (changed_by IN ('agent','operator')),\n  reason text,\n  occurred_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\n\nRLS Pattern A, service_role only, all 3 tables. Apply live against project tarritrix (jhiplicikizdpdsguimg). Update SCHEMA_REGISTRY.md, status APPLIED AND LIVE-VERIFIED. Run pnpm tsc --noEmit. Commit and push."
  gates:
  - type: compile
  - type: file_exists
    files:
    - path: SCHEMA_REGISTRY.md
      path_class: shared_canonical
- id: a40-senior-002
  name: A-40 Full Implementation - State Machine, A-45/A-13 Coordination, Human-Action Detection
  prompt: "Read A-45's real opportunity-scoring implementation and A-13's real unlinked-mention detection (brand_mentions.is_linked=false rows) - both confirmed built earlier this session - and the schema from the previous prompt first. Reuse A-45's real scoring-weight pattern for consistency rather than inventing a second scoring philosophy.\n\nImplement src/lib/agents/a-40-external-signal-coordination-engine.ts as a BaseAgent subclass:\n\ninterface A40Input {\n  client_id: string;\n}\n\ninterface A40Output {\n  status: 'COMPLETED' | 'PARTIALLY_COMPLETED';\n  opportunities_discovered: number;\n  opportunities_rejected_spam: number;\n  human_action_tasks_created: number;\n  citation_discrepancies_found: number;\n}\n\nSTATE MACHINE (real, explicit transition map, matching A-30's proven state-machine pattern from earlier tonight - reuse that exact architectural approach): lifecycle_status must follow discovered -> validated -> prioritized -> (operator_action_required -> submitted -> pending -> approved -> live) OR (rejected at any point) OR (expired from live). Implement validateTransition() rejecting any jump not in this explicit map, exactly matching how A-30 enforces its own state machine.\n\nPIPELINE:\n\n1. discoverOpportunities(client_id): reuse the shared SERP/search client (established by A-13/A-47 earlier this session - import it, do not duplicate) to search for real chamber of commerce, trade association, and directory opportunities relevant to the client's real industry and service area (pull these from the clients table, do not hardcode). This is real search-based discovery, not a static hardcoded list.\n\n2. rejectSpamAndLowQuality(candidates): apply real, checkable rejection heuristics - a directory requiring payment with no editorial review, a domain with no real organizational identity, duplicate submissions to the same directory network under different names. Write a clear rejection reason for anything filtered, do not just silently drop candidates (log what was rejected and why for auditability).\n\n3. validateOpportunity(candidate): for surviving candidates, verify the organization is real (the search result itself resolving to a genuine organizational site, not a link-farm aggregator) before marking lifecycle_status='validated'.\n\n4. scoreOpportunity(opportunity): compute all 7 named scores (legitimacy, relevance, geographic_strength, topical_strength, authority, expected_seo_value, difficulty) plus compliance_risk_score, and a composite_priority_score as a real weighted formula - state the weights explicitly and justify them in a code comment.\n\n5. detectRequiredHumanAction(opportunity): if submission genuinely requires an application, membership fee, legal agreement, or account creation (real, checkable by the opportunity_source type - e.g. chamber_of_commerce membership almost always requires a fee/application, a simple directory listing might not), set requires_human_action=true, lifecycle_status='operator_action_required', and write a specific, actionable human_action_detail (not a vague 'contact them' - real next steps: what to submit, likely cost range if discoverable, the actual URL).\n\n6. checkCitationConsistency(client_id): compare the client's real NAP (name/address/phone from the clients table) against any citation data already discovered, write citation_consistency_check rows flagging real discrepancies.\n\n7. coordinateWithA45AndA13(client_id): query A-45's backlink_opportunity_queue for unlinked_mention-type opportunities and A-13's brand_mentions where is_linked=false - these are real, already-detected candidates for reclamation, not duplicate discovery work. Cross-reference rather than re-searching for what those agents already found.\n\n8. NEVER auto-complete an opportunity to 'live' status without independent verification (per the closed-loop principle applied in A-43) - lifecycle_status only advances to 'live' via an explicit operator confirmation action in a later trigger, this agent's own run() must never self-report something as live.\n\n9. Full Contract 69 error capture, write every status transition to external_signal_lifecycle_log with changed_by='agent'.\n\nCreate src/app/api/agents/a-40/trigger/route.ts, standard operator auth, plus a second endpoint or a distinct input mode for an operator to advance an opportunity's lifecycle_status manually (submitted/approved/live/rejected) - writing to external_signal_lifecycle_log with changed_by='operator'.\n\nTEST MATRIX in tests/unit/agents/a-40.test.ts:\n- Real discovery via the shared search client returning candidates\n- Spam/low-quality rejection with real, logged reasons\n- State machine rejects an illegal transition (e.g. discovered directly to live)\n- Human-action detection correctly triggers for a membership-fee-type opportunity, not for a simple directory listing\n- Coordination correctly cross-references A-45/A-13 data without re-discovering it (assert the shared search client was NOT called again for opportunities A-45/A-13 already found)\n- Citation consistency check correctly flags a real NAP mismatch\n\nRun pnpm tsc --noEmit and pnpm vitest run tests/unit/agents/a-40.test.ts - both clean. Check agent_name enum and permission-matrix sync proactively.\n\nUpdate STATE_OF_THE_BUILD.md and AGENTS.md, SHIPPED+WIRED, noting the real coordination with A-45/A-13 and confirming this agent never self-certifies a 'live' status.\n\nCommit and push."
  gates:
  - type: compile
  - type: file_exists
    files:
    - src/lib/agents/a-40-external-signal-coordination-engine.ts
    - src/app/api/agents/a-40/trigger/route.ts
    - tests/unit/agents/a-40.test.ts
